  "question": "Let $A = \\{1,2,3\\}$ and $R_1 = \\{(a,b) : a - b$ is divisible by 3$\\}$; $R_2 = \\{(a,b): \\{a, b\\} \\subseteq \\{1\\}, \\{2\\}, \\{3\\}\\}$. Prove that $R_1 = R_2$ and both are equivalence relations. Find all equivalence classes.",
